# Domain and use cases

- Use the language and invariants in `docs/DOMAIN.md`.
- Domain code must not import Next.js, React, Zod, Drizzle, database types, or infrastructure code.
- Protect invariants when constructing or changing domain state.
- Value objects are immutable.
- Money never uses floating-point arithmetic.
- Domain errors express business meaning, not HTTP status codes.
- Name use cases after intentions such as `RegisterVisit`; do not create generic application CRUD services.
- Use named input/output types instead of long primitive parameter lists.
- Inject dependencies through application-owned ports.
- Keep transactions explicit for write use cases.
- Do not introduce base entities, serializers, or generic service interfaces before at least two real consumers justify them.

Every new or changed business rule requires an automated test.
